{
 "__doc__": [
  "Every declaration the Armory sheet renders for theme `abyss`, as",
  "(selector -> property -> value).  Review G, M9: the value half of the",
  "port had no gate, so the claim 'everything outside the nearest-token",
  "map renders byte-for-byte as before' was true and unfalsifiable once",
  "ItemDatabase/styles.qss was deleted in the same commit -- the selector",
  "NAMES survived as a snapshot, the VALUES did not.",
  "",
  "`legacy` (190 selectors) is NOT a snapshot of the current render.  It",
  "was generated by replaying the substitution map documented in the",
  "header of ItemDatabase/styles.template.qss ('NEAREST-TOKEN MAP', parts",
  "1 and 2) onto `git show eb53cd6:ItemDatabase/styles.qss`, and rendering",
  "the result for abyss.  So a failure means the render drifted from the",
  "sheet it replaced, not merely from yesterday.",
  "",
  "`added` (228 selectors) is the rules that replaced the 94 inline",
  "stylesheets.  They have no pre-image in the old file, so this half can",
  "only be a change detector -- which is what the pink->violet substat",
  "drift (review G, M10) needed and did not have.",
  "",
  "TO REGENERATE: replay that map yourself -- the template header is the",
  "authoritative copy and this fixture is downstream of it -- diff against",
  "the current render, and only then write the new values.  Never",
  "regenerate to turn a red test green without reading the diff first.",
  "",
  "One deliberate deviation from a mechanical replay is baked in:",
  "#DetailIcon keeps a translucent wash ({fg.muted|0.25}) where the rule",
  "would give a solid, for the reason the header states."
 ],
